      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Two one-dimensional (1D) helical coordination polymers, CuBIm-Cl and CuBIm-Br (BIm = 1,2-bis((5H-imidazol-4-yl)-methylene)hydrazine), are constructed from Cu2+ ions, halides and mono-deprotonated BIm. Solid-state crystalline conversions of CuBIm-Cl and CuBIm-Br to a gyroidal metal-organic framework (MOF) STU-3 which is composed of Cu ions and Bim ligands are observed through a gas-solid reaction, where the gas is methylamine."},
